            <listPerson>
                <person xml:id="TAY03" sex="1">
                    <persName>
                        <roleName/>
                        <forename>William</forename>
                        <surname>Taylor</surname>
                        <addName/>
                    </persName>
                    <birth when="1765-11-07">
                        <placeName> </placeName>
                    </birth>
                    <death when="1836-03-05"/>
                    <occupation>reviewer</occupation>
                    <occupation>translator</occupation>
                    <note type="editorial">
                        <p>William Taylor was a prominent figure in dissenting and whiggish circles in Norwich.  He was also a regular writer for the <title>Monthly Reviewer</title> and
    was acknowledged as a leading Germanist. In 1789 he was involved in the movement to repeal the Test and Corporation Acts and in 1790 he founded the Norwich 
    Revolution Society and conducted its correspondence.</p>
                        <p>All instances of 'W Taylor' in the diary have been coded as William and some instances of 'Taylor' may refer to him also; see discussion under 
  <persName key="TAY01">John Taylor</persName>.</p>
                    </note>
                    <bibl type="other">David Chandler, <title>Norwich Literature, 1788-97: A Critical Survey</title> (unpub. Oxford D.Phil. thesis, 1997).</bibl>
                    <bibl type="other"><title>DNB</title>.</bibl>
                </person>
            </listPerson>
